{"authored" [{"question" "q-75205" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the curve $r(t)=⟨{t}^{2}-1\\,,\\,{t}^{3}+1⟩,t\\in (-\\infty ,0)$ find all of the points at which the tangent to the curve is perpendicular to the vector $⟨2\\,,\\,1⟩.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14078039/state.json" "file_sha256" "6993b78098630c40ef25db159f41ec7e39ae10b153daa72518072cd5444660be" "basis" 2814 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14078039/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-75205" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we calculate the derivative of $r(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}-1)\\,,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}+1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2t\\,,\\,3{t}^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vectors  $⟨2\\,,\\,1⟩$ and ${r}^{′}(t)$ are perpendicular for some value of the parameter $t$ if and only if $⟨2\\,,\\,1⟩\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)=0.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨2\\,,\\,1⟩\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) & =0 \\\\ ⟨2\\,,\\,1⟩\\cdot ⟨2t\\,,\\,3{t}^{2}⟩ & =0 \\\\ 2\\cdot 2t+1\\cdot 3{t}^{2} & =0 \\\\ 4t+3{t}^{2} & =0 \\\\ t(4+3t) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $t\\in (-\\infty ,0)$, the only solution is $t=-\\frac{4}{3}$\n\nFinally, since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(-\\frac{4}{3}) & =⟨{(-\\frac{4}{3})}^{2}-1\\,,\\,{(-\\frac{4}{3})}^{3}+1⟩=⟨\\frac{7}{9}\\,,\\,-\\frac{37}{27}⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n we conclude that $⟨2\\,,\\,-1⟩$ and ${r}^{′}(t)$ are perpendicular at the point $(\\frac{7}{9}\\,,\\,-\\frac{37}{27}).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14078039/state.json" "file_sha256" "6993b78098630c40ef25db159f41ec7e39ae10b153daa72518072cd5444660be" "basis" 2814 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14078039/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-75205" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14078039/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "943d99b88dd5ef61db0015339755f4f0ea9e8b2c195300e13bfb7ee419247aea" "basis" 2814 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14078039/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-75205" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14078039/state.json" "file_sha256" "6993b78098630c40ef25db159f41ec7e39ae10b153daa72518072cd5444660be" "basis" 2814 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14078039/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-75205" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "(0,0)"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14078039/state.json" "file_sha256" "6993b78098630c40ef25db159f41ec7e39ae10b153daa72518072cd5444660be" "basis" 2814 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14078039/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-75205" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "(\\frac{4}{3}\\,,\\,\\frac{16}{9})"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14078039/state.json" "file_sha256" "6993b78098630c40ef25db159f41ec7e39ae10b153daa72518072cd5444660be" "basis" 2814 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14078039/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-75205" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "(\\frac{7}{9}\\,,\\,-\\frac{37}{27})"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14078039/state.json" "file_sha256" "6993b78098630c40ef25db159f41ec7e39ae10b153daa72518072cd5444660be" "basis" 2814 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14078039/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-75205" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "$(0,0)$ and $(\\frac{4}{3}\\,,\\,\\frac{16}{9})$"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14078039/state.json" "file_sha256" "6993b78098630c40ef25db159f41ec7e39ae10b153daa72518072cd5444660be" "basis" 2814 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14078039/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-75205" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "$(3,-7)$ and $(\\frac{7}{9}\\,,\\,-\\frac{37}{27})$"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14078039/state.json" "file_sha256" "6993b78098630c40ef25db159f41ec7e39ae10b153daa72518072cd5444660be" "basis" 2814 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14078039/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-75205" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(\\frac{7}{9}\\,,\\,-\\frac{37}{27})"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14078039/state.json" "file_sha256" "6993b78098630c40ef25db159f41ec7e39ae10b153daa72518072cd5444660be" "basis" 2814 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14078039/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-165040" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the curve $r(t)=⟨{t}^{2}-2t\\,,\\,{t}^{2}\\,,\\,8t-2{t}^{2}⟩,$ find the point at which the tangent to the curve is parallel to the vector $⟨1\\,,\\,2\\,,\\,0⟩.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14078039/state.json" "file_sha256" "6993b78098630c40ef25db159f41ec7e39ae10b153daa72518072cd5444660be" "basis" 2814 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14078039/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-165040" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we calculate the derivative of $r(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}-2t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(8t-2{t}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2t-2,\\,2t,\\,8-4t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vectors ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $⟨0\\,,\\,1\\,,\\,3⟩$ are parallel for some specific value ${t}_{0}$ of the parameter $t$ if and only if there exists a constant $c$ such that ${r}^{′}({t}_{0})=c\\,⟨1\\,,\\,2\\,,\\,0⟩.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =c\\,⟨1\\,,\\,2\\,,\\,0⟩ \\\\ ⟨2t-2,\\,2t,\\,8-4t⟩ & =c\\,⟨1\\,,\\,2\\,,\\,0⟩ \\\\ ⟨2t-2,\\,2t,\\,8-4t⟩ & =⟨c\\,,\\,2c\\,,\\,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the components gives:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2t-2=c \\\\ 2t=2c \\\\ 8-4t=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we obtain that $t=2.$ Substituting to the second equation, we get $c=2.$\nThese values also satisfy the first equation. \n\nTherefore, $⟨1\\,,\\,2\\,,\\,0⟩$ and ${r}^{′}$ are parallel only at the point corresponding to $t=2.$\n\nFinally, since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(2) & =⟨{2}^{2}-2(2)\\,,\\,{2}^{2}\\,,\\,8(2)-2(2)^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,4,\\,8⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe conclude that $⟨1\\,,\\,2\\,,\\,0⟩$ and ${r}^{′}(t)$ are parallel at the point $(0,4,8).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14078039/state.json" "file_sha256" "6993b78098630c40ef25db159f41ec7e39ae10b153daa72518072cd5444660be" "basis" 2814 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14078039/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-165040" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14078039/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "943d99b88dd5ef61db0015339755f4f0ea9e8b2c195300e13bfb7ee419247aea" "basis" 2814 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14078039/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-165040" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14078039/state.json" "file_sha256" "6993b78098630c40ef25db159f41ec7e39ae10b153daa72518072cd5444660be" "basis" 2814 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14078039/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-165040" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "(-1,1,6)"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14078039/state.json" "file_sha256" "6993b78098630c40ef25db159f41ec7e39ae10b153daa72518072cd5444660be" "basis" 2814 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14078039/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-165040" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "(0,4,8)"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14078039/state.json" "file_sha256" "6993b78098630c40ef25db159f41ec7e39ae10b153daa72518072cd5444660be" "basis" 2814 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14078039/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-165040" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "(3,1,-10)"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14078039/state.json" "file_sha256" "6993b78098630c40ef25db159f41ec7e39ae10b153daa72518072cd5444660be" "basis" 2814 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14078039/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-165040" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "$(0,0,0)$ and $(0,4,8)$"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14078039/state.json" "file_sha256" "6993b78098630c40ef25db159f41ec7e39ae10b153daa72518072cd5444660be" "basis" 2814 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14078039/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-165040" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "$(3,1,-10)$ and $(-1,1,6)$"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14078039/state.json" "file_sha256" "6993b78098630c40ef25db159f41ec7e39ae10b153daa72518072cd5444660be" "basis" 2814 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14078039/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-32876" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following gives the equation of the tangent to the curve $r(t)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi t\\,j+t\\,k$ at the point $P(-1,0,\\frac{3}{2}),$ valid for real values of $u?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083270/state.json" "file_sha256" "793bd7002525f88c0b685a198519f47da2a172c6990e043c104414fcaf32f7e0"} {"question" "q-32876" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The point $P(-1,0,\\frac{3}{2})$ is at the tip of $r(t)$ for some specific value ${t}_{0}$ of the parameter $t.$ At this point,  the vector ${r}^{′}({t}_{0})$ is tangent to the curve, so the tangent line to the curve at $P$ can be parametrized as\n\n$$\nR(u)=r({t}_{0})+u\\,{r}^{′}({t}_{0}),\\,u\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\n \n\nFirst, we find the value of $t$ that corresponds to $P.$ We know that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =-i+0\\,j+\\frac{3}{2}\\,k \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi t\\,j+t\\,k & =-i+0\\,j+\\frac{3}{2}\\,k,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand equating the coefficients of $i,j,$ and $k$ yields the following system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi t=-1 \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi t=0 \\\\ t=\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first equation, we get $t=\\frac{3}{2}.$ This value also satisfies the other two equations. Therefore, $P(-1,0,\\frac{3}{2})$ is at the tip of the vector $r(\\frac{3}{2}).$  \n\nWe calculate ${r}^{′}(t):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\,k \\\\  & =\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi t\\,i-\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi t\\,j+\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we evaluate ${r}^{′}(t)$ at $t=\\frac{3}{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(\\frac{3}{2}) & =\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})\\,i-\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})\\,j+\\,k \\\\  & =0\\,i+\\pi \\,j+\\,k \\\\  & =\\pi \\,j+\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the tangent line to the given curve at the point $P(-1,0,\\frac{3}{2})$ is\n\n$$\nR(u)=-i+\\frac{3}{2}\\,k+u\\,(\\pi \\,j+\\,k),\\,u\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083270/state.json" "file_sha256" "793bd7002525f88c0b685a198519f47da2a172c6990e043c104414fcaf32f7e0"} {"question" "q-32876" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083270/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "03cbb8af73d195e2bc9de750bf95e2fbcc8f856913f0f90973476dc2288a0ea8"} {"question" "q-32876" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083270/state.json" "file_sha256" "793bd7002525f88c0b685a198519f47da2a172c6990e043c104414fcaf32f7e0"} {"question" "q-32876" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-i+\\frac{3}{2}\\,k+u(-\\pi \\,j-\\,k)"] ["math" "-i+\\frac{3}{2}\\,k+u(\\pi \\,i+\\,j)"] ["math" "-i+\\frac{3}{2}\\,k+u(\\pi \\,j+\\,k)"] ["math" "-i+\\frac{3}{2}\\,k+u(i+\\pi \\,j+\\,k)"] ["math" "-i-\\frac{3}{2}\\,k+u(\\pi \\,i+\\,k)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083270/state.json" "file_sha256" "793bd7002525f88c0b685a198519f47da2a172c6990e043c104414fcaf32f7e0"} {"question" "q-32876" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-i+\\frac{3}{2}\\,k+u(\\pi \\,j+\\,k)"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083270/state.json" "file_sha256" "793bd7002525f88c0b685a198519f47da2a172c6990e043c104414fcaf32f7e0"} {"question" "q-75205" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the curve $r(t)=⟨{t}^{2}-1\\,,\\,{t}^{3}+1⟩,t\\in (-\\infty ,0)$ find all of the points at which the tangent to the curve is perpendicular to the vector $⟨2\\,,\\,1⟩.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083270/state.json" "file_sha256" "793bd7002525f88c0b685a198519f47da2a172c6990e043c104414fcaf32f7e0"} {"question" "q-75205" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we calculate the derivative of $r(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}-1)\\,,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}+1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2t\\,,\\,3{t}^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vectors  $⟨2\\,,\\,1⟩$ and ${r}^{′}(t)$ are perpendicular for some value of the parameter $t$ if and only if $⟨2\\,,\\,1⟩\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)=0.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨2\\,,\\,1⟩\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) & =0 \\\\ ⟨2\\,,\\,1⟩\\cdot ⟨2t\\,,\\,3{t}^{2}⟩ & =0 \\\\ 2\\cdot 2t+1\\cdot 3{t}^{2} & =0 \\\\ 4t+3{t}^{2} & =0 \\\\ t(4+3t) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $t\\in (-\\infty ,0)$, the only solution is $t=-\\frac{4}{3}$\n\nFinally, since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(-\\frac{4}{3}) & =⟨{(-\\frac{4}{3})}^{2}-1\\,,\\,{(-\\frac{4}{3})}^{3}+1⟩=⟨\\frac{7}{9}\\,,\\,-\\frac{37}{27}⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n we conclude that $⟨2\\,,\\,-1⟩$ and ${r}^{′}(t)$ are perpendicular at the point $(\\frac{7}{9}\\,,\\,-\\frac{37}{27}).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083270/state.json" "file_sha256" "793bd7002525f88c0b685a198519f47da2a172c6990e043c104414fcaf32f7e0"} {"question" "q-75205" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083270/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "03cbb8af73d195e2bc9de750bf95e2fbcc8f856913f0f90973476dc2288a0ea8"} {"question" "q-75205" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083270/state.json" "file_sha256" "793bd7002525f88c0b685a198519f47da2a172c6990e043c104414fcaf32f7e0"} {"question" "q-75205" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(0,0)"] ["math" "(\\frac{4}{3}\\,,\\,\\frac{16}{9})"] ["math" "(\\frac{7}{9}\\,,\\,-\\frac{37}{27})"] ["text" "$(0,0)$ and $(\\frac{4}{3}\\,,\\,\\frac{16}{9})$"] ["text" "$(3,-7)$ and $(\\frac{7}{9}\\,,\\,-\\frac{37}{27})$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083270/state.json" "file_sha256" "793bd7002525f88c0b685a198519f47da2a172c6990e043c104414fcaf32f7e0"} {"question" "q-75205" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(\\frac{7}{9}\\,,\\,-\\frac{37}{27})"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083270/state.json" "file_sha256" "793bd7002525f88c0b685a198519f47da2a172c6990e043c104414fcaf32f7e0"} {"question" "q-75524" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the curve $r(t)=⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,,\\,3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩,t\\in [0,\\pi )$ find all of the points at which ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $r(t)$ are perpendicular." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083270/state.json" "file_sha256" "793bd7002525f88c0b685a198519f47da2a172c6990e043c104414fcaf32f7e0"} {"question" "q-75524" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we calculate the derivative of $r(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,,\\,-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vectors  $r(t)$ and ${r}^{′}(t)$ are perpendicular for some value of the parameter $t$ if and only if $r(t)\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)=0.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t)\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) & =0 \\\\ ⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,,\\,3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩\\cdot ⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,,\\,-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩ & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡t+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\cdot (-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t) & =0 \\\\ -8\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡2t & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $t\\in [0,\\pi )$, the only solutions are $t=0$ and $t=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$\n\nFinally, since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(0) & =⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡0\\,,\\,3\\operatorname{cos}⁡0⟩=⟨0\\,,\\,3⟩, \\\\ r(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\,,\\,3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{2}⟩=⟨1\\,,\\,0⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n we conclude that $r(t)$ and ${r}^{′}(t)$ are perpendicular at the points $(0,3)$ and $(1,0).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083270/state.json" "file_sha256" "793bd7002525f88c0b685a198519f47da2a172c6990e043c104414fcaf32f7e0"} {"question" "q-75524" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083270/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "03cbb8af73d195e2bc9de750bf95e2fbcc8f856913f0f90973476dc2288a0ea8"} {"question" "q-75524" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083270/state.json" "file_sha256" "793bd7002525f88c0b685a198519f47da2a172c6990e043c104414fcaf32f7e0"} {"question" "q-75524" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(1,0)"] ["math" "(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},-\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2})"] ["text" "$(0,3)$ and $(1,0)$"] ["text" "$(0,3)$ and $(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},-\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2})$"] ["text" "$(1,0)$ and $(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2},-\\frac{3}{2})$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083270/state.json" "file_sha256" "793bd7002525f88c0b685a198519f47da2a172c6990e043c104414fcaf32f7e0"} {"question" "q-75524" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$(0,3)$ and $(1,0)$"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083270/state.json" "file_sha256" "793bd7002525f88c0b685a198519f47da2a172c6990e043c104414fcaf32f7e0"} {"question" "q-126837" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following gives the equation of the tangent to the curve $r(t)=⟨{t}^{3},{t}^{2}-2⟩$ at the point where $t=3,$  valid for all  real values of $u?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083270/state.json" "file_sha256" "793bd7002525f88c0b685a198519f47da2a172c6990e043c104414fcaf32f7e0"} {"question" "q-126837" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "At the point where $t=3,$ the vector ${r}^{′}(3)$ is tangent to the curve, so the tangent line to the curve at $P$ can be parametrized as\n \n\n$$\nR(u)=r(3)+u{r}^{′}(3),\\,u\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\n$$\n\n \n\nFirst, we find $r(3):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(3) & =⟨{3}^{3},{3}^{2}-2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨27,7⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n   \n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{′}(t):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}-2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3{t}^{2},2t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we evaluate ${r}^{′}(t)$ at $t=3:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(3) & =⟨3(3)^{2},2(3)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨27,6⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the tangent line to the given curve at the point where $t=3$ is\n\n$$\nR(u)=⟨27,7⟩+u⟨27,6⟩,\\,u\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083270/state.json" "file_sha256" "793bd7002525f88c0b685a198519f47da2a172c6990e043c104414fcaf32f7e0"} {"question" "q-126837" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083270/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "03cbb8af73d195e2bc9de750bf95e2fbcc8f856913f0f90973476dc2288a0ea8"} {"question" "q-126837" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083270/state.json" "file_sha256" "793bd7002525f88c0b685a198519f47da2a172c6990e043c104414fcaf32f7e0"} {"question" "q-126837" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨27,7⟩+u⟨14,6⟩"] ["math" "⟨27,7⟩+u⟨27,6⟩"] ["math" "⟨27,7⟩+u⟨9,7⟩"] ["math" "⟨9,1⟩+u⟨27,6⟩"] ["math" "⟨9,1⟩+u⟨9,7⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083270/state.json" "file_sha256" "793bd7002525f88c0b685a198519f47da2a172c6990e043c104414fcaf32f7e0"} {"question" "q-126837" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨27,7⟩+u⟨27,6⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083270/state.json" "file_sha256" "793bd7002525f88c0b685a198519f47da2a172c6990e043c104414fcaf32f7e0"} {"question" "q-165040" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the curve $r(t)=⟨{t}^{2}-2t\\,,\\,{t}^{2}\\,,\\,8t-2{t}^{2}⟩,$ find the point at which the tangent to the curve is parallel to the vector $⟨1\\,,\\,2\\,,\\,0⟩.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083270/state.json" "file_sha256" "793bd7002525f88c0b685a198519f47da2a172c6990e043c104414fcaf32f7e0"} {"question" "q-165040" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we calculate the derivative of $r(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}-2t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(8t-2{t}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2t-2,\\,2t,\\,8-4t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vectors ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $⟨0\\,,\\,1\\,,\\,3⟩$ are parallel for some specific value ${t}_{0}$ of the parameter $t$ if and only if there exists a constant $c$ such that ${r}^{′}({t}_{0})=c\\,⟨1\\,,\\,2\\,,\\,0⟩.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =c\\,⟨1\\,,\\,2\\,,\\,0⟩ \\\\ ⟨2t-2,\\,2t,\\,8-4t⟩ & =c\\,⟨1\\,,\\,2\\,,\\,0⟩ \\\\ ⟨2t-2,\\,2t,\\,8-4t⟩ & =⟨c\\,,\\,2c\\,,\\,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the components gives:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2t-2=c \\\\ 2t=2c \\\\ 8-4t=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we obtain that $t=2.$ Substituting to the second equation, we get $c=2.$\nThese values also satisfy the first equation. \n\nTherefore, $⟨1\\,,\\,2\\,,\\,0⟩$ and ${r}^{′}$ are parallel only at the point corresponding to $t=2.$\n\nFinally, since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(2) & =⟨{2}^{2}-2(2)\\,,\\,{2}^{2}\\,,\\,8(2)-2(2)^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,4,\\,8⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe conclude that $⟨1\\,,\\,2\\,,\\,0⟩$ and ${r}^{′}(t)$ are parallel at the point $(0,4,8).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083270/state.json" "file_sha256" "793bd7002525f88c0b685a198519f47da2a172c6990e043c104414fcaf32f7e0"} {"question" "q-165040" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083270/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "03cbb8af73d195e2bc9de750bf95e2fbcc8f856913f0f90973476dc2288a0ea8"} {"question" "q-165040" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083270/state.json" "file_sha256" "793bd7002525f88c0b685a198519f47da2a172c6990e043c104414fcaf32f7e0"} {"question" "q-165040" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(-1,1,6)"] ["math" "(0,4,8)"] ["math" "(3,1,-10)"] ["text" "$(0,0,0)$ and $(0,4,8)$"] ["text" "$(3,1,-10)$ and $(-1,1,6)$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083270/state.json" "file_sha256" "793bd7002525f88c0b685a198519f47da2a172c6990e043c104414fcaf32f7e0"} {"question" "q-165040" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(0,4,8)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083270/state.json" "file_sha256" "793bd7002525f88c0b685a198519f47da2a172c6990e043c104414fcaf32f7e0"}] "usage" {"q-165040" [] "q-75205" []} "basis" 2872 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [17592186384831 17592186384832 17592186384833 17592186384834 17592186384835 17592186384866 17592186384867 17592186384868 17592186384869 17592186384870] "immutable_fields" [[17592186384830 :answer-field/correct] [17592186384830 :answer-field/id] [17592186384830 :answer-field/key] [17592186384830 :answer-field/type] [17592186384865 :answer-field/correct] [17592186384865 :answer-field/id] [17592186384865 :answer-field/key] [17592186384865 :answer-field/type